'''''Atrichum angustatum''''', commonly known as '''slender starburst moss''',<ref>{{cite web |title=Digital Atlas of Virginia Flora |url=https://vaplantatlas.org/index.php?do=plant&plant=3981 |access-date=26 October 2024}}</ref> is a species of [[mosses]] belonging to the family [[Polytrichaceae]].<ref name="worldfloraonline.org">{{cite web |title=Atrichum angustatum (Brid.) Bruch & Schimp. |url=http://www.worldfloraonline.org/taxon/wfo-0001192382 |website=www.worldfloraonline.org |access-date=28 January 2021}}</ref>

It is native to [[Eurasia]] and [[Northern America]].<ref name="GBIF">{{cite web |title=Atrichum angustatum Bruch & W.P.Schimper, 1844 |url=https://www.gbif.org/species/2682949 |website=www.gbif.org |access-date=28 January 2021 |language=en}}</ref> It is rare in [[Iceland]], being found at only two locations; there, it is locally listed as a [[vulnerable species]] (VU).<ref Name="NÍ1996">Náttúrufræðistofnun Íslands [Icelandic Institute of Natural History] (1996). ''[http://utgafa.ni.is/valistar/valisti_1.pdf Válisti 1: Plöntur.]'' (in Icelandic) Reykjavík: Náttúrufræðistofnun Íslands.</ref>

